flowchart LR
  CLIENT[Customer app<br/>OTel client span + W3C traceparent] --> CF[CloudFront<br/>edge metrics, logs, request ID]
  CF --> WAF[AWS WAF<br/>native metrics/logs]
  WAF --> API[API Gateway<br/>managed X-Ray trace optional]
  API --> EKS[EKS services<br/>OTel instrumentation]
  EKS --> AUR[Aurora<br/>native metrics + Database Insights]
  EKS --> MSK[MSK<br/>native broker/lag metrics]
  EKS --> EXT[External API client spans]
  MSK --> CONSUMER[Consumer OTel spans<br/>context from message headers]
  CF -. X-Amz-Cf-Id / edge request ID correlation .-> EKS

  EKS --> COLLECTOR[ADOT / CloudWatch agent<br/>OTel collection]
  CONSUMER --> COLLECTOR
  COLLECTOR --> APP[CloudWatch Application Signals<br/>service health, SLOs, application map]
  COLLECTOR --> TRACE[AWS X-Ray service<br/>Trace Map + Transaction Search]
  API -. managed trace where enabled .-> TRACE
  CF -. edge logs and timing .-> EDGELOG[CloudWatch edge telemetry]
  AUR -. DB load/wait/query evidence .-> DBI[CloudWatch Database Insights]
  MSK -. broker/consumer lag .-> CW[CloudWatch native service metrics]
  WAF --> CW
  CI[CloudWatch Container Insights] --> CW

  SYN[CloudWatch Synthetics<br/>sign-in, balance, payment preflight] --> APP
  RUM[CloudWatch RUM<br/>client experience, if approved] --> APP
  APP --> ALERT[Grouped alert routes<br/>journey, owner, runbook]
  TRACE --> ALERT
  LOG[CloudWatch Logs<br/>redacted + data protection masking] --> S3[Encrypted S3 archive<br/>retention per approved policy]
